  "flags": [
    {"page": 2, "what": "A thespian troupe needs at least three models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported."},
    {"page": 5, "what": "The PDF has no Special column, and its five new skills each name one of the standard lists instead, so the warband brings no skill group of its own: Elusive joins Combat, Wilhelm Tellus Shooting, Starstruck Academic, Rough and Tumble Strength and Celebrity Speed, each in the Grade 3 setting."},
    {"page": 5, "what": "The skill table was read from the page's own text columns (Combat 30, Shooting 48, Academic 66, Strength 83, Speed 100). No page was opened as an image."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "The Marquee players (Narrator, Villain, Authority, Protagonist, Sidekick) are the heroes: they have the skill table and their own starting experience. The Minor players (Fight Masters, Soldiers, Forest Kin, Townsfolk) all start with 0 and are the henchmen."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "A troupe must hold at least one Fight Master and no more than two, so the group is imported as 1-2."},
    {"page": 6, "what": "The Marksman Equipment List is headed \"for Marksmen only\" but the PDF has no Marksman; the Forest Kin are the only fighters sent to it, so it is theirs."},
    {"page": 6, "what": "The Rapier is 15 gc here and ours is 15 gc Rare 5 but open to eight other warbands, so the troupe gets a price row. The Duelling pistol is 25 gc (50 for a brace) against our 30 (60), and the Hunting rifle, Blunderbuss, Handgun and Pistol are ours at the same prices."},
    {"page": 6, "what": "\"Mace/Club\" is read as our Mace, \"Spear/Pitchfork\" as our Spear, \"Halberd/Bill/Scythe\" as our Halberd and \"Helmet/Pot\" as our Helmet, each shown under the list's own wording."},
    {"page": 7, "what": "The Thespian spell list is imported as the lore Thespian Magic: Scripted 9, Soliloquy 11, Our Story Thus Far 10. The Narrator casts from it or from Lesser Magic, as the PDF allows."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "No group sizes are printed except the Townsfolk's 2-5."}
  ]
